{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105593-running-fomorians","id":1105593,"title":"Running Fomorians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-19T21:46:51-07:00","id":1105593,"title":"Running Fomorians","content":"How to I ST a Fomorian? I was using the Gentry from Autumn Nightmares then tweaking it with C20, Infernalism: Path of Scream, Earthbound and nWoD: Inferno. My understanding is the White Court represents intellectual evil. I don't know if that would work for wrath and lust. That might be the Green Court's more primal proclivities. The Red Court technically rules over wrath, but since the world's ending, Banality have blurred things somewhat. Help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:42:12-07:00","id":1106236,"title":"","content":"I pick a concept, one that covers a primal fear of man (My personal favorites were &quot;creature outside of the village/campfire&quot;, or &quot;starvation&quot;) and use that as a theme. These are things of vast power, akin to demons, and should be treated as capable of vast and terrible thematic alteration in the Dreaming, where their power should first be displayed. If looking toward the mundane realm, terrorist attacks, a steep rise in crime, war breaking out.... Whatever makes people afraid to go outside are appropriate for the Autumn world. The key factor to addressing them is whatever invokes fear and nightmares in the mind of the dreamers strengthens Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Fighting a Fomorian is likely about as easy as stopping those events in the Autumn world, too. You might approach the Fomorian in the Dreaming, but unless they are inclined to talk (and strangely, White and Green tend to) this route is likely to result in PC death, assuming they have not achieved the sort of power that could suitably stand against such things if they worked together. Treasures, such as the Triumph Cask, are likely a great idea for possible victory solutions, and the acquisition of such a treasure could be the basis of an entire first act of the game, seeing as the Fomorians are just as likely to want such things for themselves, and are likely to send groups of Thallian after them.<br /> <br /> To simplify the courts (and for note, running them as 3 separate forces that rarely work together is encouraged, they represent wildly different visions for the Dreaming) here are the themes they invoked for me:<br /> <br /> White Court: Beautiful Lies, Treachery, Manipulation, Depicting unwholesome acts as normal or casual, Cold and casual evil, Machiavellian politics.<br /> <br /> Green Court: Atavistic rituals, Lovecraftian symbolism, The Unknown, Forbidden Knowledge, Madness, Ignorance, Loss of self, Body Horror.<br /> <br /> Red Court: Destruction, War, Mindless Violence, Revolution, Collateral Damage, Torture, Domination Through Bloodshed, Tyranny.<br /> <br /> Obviously, each of these have fears associated with them, along with imagery. White, for me, came with images of forests covered in spider webs, constant whispering all around you, and a sense of being maliciously watched. Green had more to do with the Sea, and thus lighthouses, things roiling under water, and slow descents into madness were my depiction. Red was all fire, blood and death. Battlefields, or what was left afterwards, featured heavily in depictions for me.<br /> <br /> In the end, I advise working with things you know people are afraid of, and determine which direction you want to go. The Great Winter Wolf was my last, and it was Green Court, representing people's primal fears of what creatures lay outside their homes, waiting to feast upon them. It worked out well.Go with what works for your table, and it should be awesome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11773-shining-imperator","name":"Shining Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:53:39-07:00","id":1111754,"title":"","content":"The Fomorian embodies Lust and Wrath. Very cold and calculating. Indulging in rape isn't as fun as seducing someone. Appearance and weapons aside, still working on it. Thanks for the help. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}